WEBVTT

00:00:00.692 --> 00:00:10.069
His family name is Edson Arrantes Donasciemento, but people call him, Helé.

00:00:10.129 --> 00:00:15.182
He is the number one player in the story of soccer.

00:00:15.242 --> 00:00:21.685
In 1363 games, he scored 1264 goals.

00:00:21.745 --> 00:00:30.398
With Brazil, he won the World Cup three times.

00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:37.252
He visited 88 countries, and his picture was in every newspaper.

00:00:37.312 --> 00:00:42.024
But Pele is not only a famous soccer player.

00:00:42.084 --> 00:00:47.947
He knows Spanish, Italian, English, and French.

00:00:48.007 --> 00:00:53.668
He writes music, and he works for the Brazilian government.

00:00:53.728 --> 00:00:57.427
Today, Helene is famous.

00:00:57.487 --> 00:01:03.979
In 1950, he was a boy of 10 with no shoes.

00:01:04.038 --> 00:01:07.359
This is his story.

00:01:07.419 --> 00:01:10.010
Early years.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:17.462
Edson Arrante's Donasimento came into the world on the night of October 23rd, 1940.

00:01:17.482 --> 00:01:21.342
His family called him Dico.

00:01:21.402 --> 00:01:29.554
They lived in a small house in Tres Corsois, Brazil.

00:01:29.613 --> 00:01:34.946
Dico has soccer players' legs, his father said.

00:01:35.006 --> 00:01:39.428
He's going to be a doctor, not a soccer player.

00:01:39.488 --> 00:01:42.438
Dico's mother Celeste said.

00:01:42.498 --> 00:01:45.670
Celeste was angry.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:53.220
Don Dino, Dico's father, was a soccer player, but he didn't make much money.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.879
Dondino smiled.

00:01:55.939 --> 00:02:04.374
There were problems in the family about soccer, but there was a lot of love in the house, too.

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:13.360
In 1944, the manager of Baru Atletical, a big soccer club, talked to Dondino.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.722
We want a good soccer player, then said.

00:02:17.782 --> 00:02:22.864
It's not much money, but there's work in the town, too.

00:02:22.924 --> 00:02:25.692
Do you want the job?"

00:02:25.752 --> 00:02:31.934
Dondino said yes, and the family moved to Baru.

00:02:31.994 --> 00:02:35.506
The manager was wrong about one thing.

00:02:35.566 --> 00:02:39.757
There was no work for Dondino in the town.

00:02:39.817 --> 00:02:46.348
He only played soccer, and the family had the same money problems.

00:02:46.408 --> 00:03:00.035
But Dica was happy in Baru with his new friends They played their first game of soccer in Rua Rubens Aruda, a street near Diko's house.

00:03:00.095 --> 00:03:04.906
Their football was an old newspaper.

00:03:04.966 --> 00:03:09.018
Little Diko played a lot of soccer.

00:03:09.078 --> 00:03:12.209
Celeste wasn't happy about this.

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:16.120
There's no money in the game, she said.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.890
Diko smiled.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.107
His mother was right.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:25.366
He loved soccer, but he didn't want to be a soccer player.

00:03:25.426 --> 00:03:28.790
He wanted to work at the airport.

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:33.032
He often went there and looked at the airplanes.

00:03:33.092 --> 00:03:39.378
But Diko's first job wasn't in a soccer stadium or an airport.

00:03:39.438 --> 00:03:42.620
It was at Barru Station in 1948.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.511
He cleaned shoes.

00:03:43.571 --> 00:03:51.606
In that year, Things were difficult for the family.

00:03:51.666 --> 00:03:57.010
But then, Dondino started work in a doctor's office.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:01.684
He cleaned the building and answered the telephone.

00:04:01.744 --> 00:04:07.507
In the afternoons, Dico often visited his father.

00:04:07.566 --> 00:04:14.972
In ten years, you're going to be a young man, Dondino said one day.

00:04:15.032 --> 00:04:18.094
What do you want to do?

00:04:18.154 --> 00:04:23.068
I want to work with airplanes," Diko said.

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:29.795
Okay, but school is important for that, said his father.

00:04:29.855 --> 00:04:34.400
Later that year, Diko started school.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.203
He wasn't a good student.

00:04:37.262 --> 00:04:42.899
He only stayed in school because he wanted a job at the airport.

00:04:42.959 --> 00:04:48.353
But one day, an airplane came down near the school.

00:04:48.413 --> 00:04:54.926
Deco and his friends went to the doctor's office and looked in one of the windows.

00:04:54.986 --> 00:04:59.137
The man from the airplane was dead.

00:04:59.197 --> 00:05:04.309
Deco never talked about a job with airplanes again.

00:05:04.369 --> 00:05:07.360
A new name.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:12.510
The important thing for Deco now was soccer.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:16.949
evenings and weekends, he played with his friends.

00:05:17.009 --> 00:05:21.412
In the afternoons, he was with Don Dino.

00:05:21.472 --> 00:05:28.866
Don Dino was his soccer teacher, and Dico was a very good student.

00:05:28.926 --> 00:05:35.259
After two years, Dico was the number one young player in Baru.

00:05:35.319 --> 00:05:40.122
His friends started to call him Pele.

00:05:40.182 --> 00:05:43.092
Where does the name come from?

00:05:43.152 --> 00:05:45.032
people often ask.

00:05:45.092 --> 00:05:47.732
Pele doesn't know.

00:05:47.792 --> 00:05:56.414
In 1951 Pele started a club September 7 with his friends.

00:05:56.474 --> 00:06:01.306
People called them the team with no shoes.

00:06:01.366 --> 00:06:10.638
They wanted to play in Baru Atletico's championship for young teams, but the shoes were a problem.

00:06:10.698 --> 00:06:16.556
One day A father of one of the players came with shoes for the team.

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:24.694
"'Day, I'm giving you a new name, Americano,' he said.

00:06:24.754 --> 00:06:30.248
Now they can't call you the team with no shoes.

00:06:30.308 --> 00:06:36.886
Americano played very well and won the championship.

00:06:36.946 --> 00:06:42.872
After the final, Don Dino looked at his son and smiled.

00:06:42.932 --> 00:06:48.574
You played a beautiful game, Diko, he said.

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:52.526
Balimar de Brito.

00:06:52.586 --> 00:06:58.288
Baru Atletical liked Pele's beautiful game too.

00:06:58.348 --> 00:07:04.881
They wanted him for the club's new team of young players, Pacino.

00:07:04.941 --> 00:07:13.159
The team manager was Voldemort de Brito, a famous man in Brazilian soccer.

00:07:13.219 --> 00:07:16.630
Pellet was very happy.

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:22.791
Voldemort was a good manager and a good teacher.

00:07:22.851 --> 00:07:29.263
In 1953, Baccino won the Baru Young Team Championship.

00:07:29.323 --> 00:07:32.914
After this, Voldemort moved away.

00:07:32.974 --> 00:07:36.221
Pellet was very sorry.

00:07:36.281 --> 00:07:43.789
One year later, Pelé finished school and started to work in a shoe factory.

00:07:43.849 --> 00:07:50.871
At weekends, he played for Baccino, but he didn't like the new manager.

00:07:50.931 --> 00:07:55.472
1954 was a bad year.

00:07:55.532 --> 00:08:01.274
In the winter of the new year, Voldemort came to Pelé's house.

00:08:01.334 --> 00:08:04.487
He wanted to talk to the family.

00:08:04.546 --> 00:08:08.620
Your son is fifteen now," he said.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:11.984
He's a very good soccer player.

00:08:12.044 --> 00:08:15.846
He can try for a job with Santos.

00:08:15.906 --> 00:08:19.398
Dondino and Pellet were happy.

00:08:19.458 --> 00:08:24.232
Santos was a very famous club in Brazil.

00:08:24.292 --> 00:08:29.394
Celeste didn't like it, but she said yes.

00:08:29.453 --> 00:08:37.096
Some days later, Don Dino and Pellet went to Santos on the train.

00:08:37.155 --> 00:08:42.589
The Santos players aren't going to like me, Pellet said.

00:08:42.649 --> 00:08:45.681
But there was no problem.

00:08:45.741 --> 00:08:51.794
Pellet played well, and the club was happy with its new player.

00:08:51.854 --> 00:08:55.066
Pellet was happy too.

00:08:55.126 --> 00:09:00.243
After some weeks, he had a good friend on the team.

00:09:00.303 --> 00:09:03.328
His name was Zito.

00:09:03.388 --> 00:09:14.886
Pallet wasn't in the first team, but one day, a first team player, Vasconcelos, had an injury.

00:09:14.946 --> 00:09:21.450
Let's put young Pallet in the first team, the manager said.

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:27.062
Pallet played well and stayed in the first team.

00:09:27.123 --> 00:09:34.554
He scored his first goal for them on September 7, 1956.

00:09:34.614 --> 00:09:39.755
After that, he started to score a lot of goals.

00:09:39.815 --> 00:09:43.246
The team were very happy.

00:09:43.306 --> 00:09:50.818
In June, 1957, they played in the Maracanya Championship.

00:09:50.878 --> 00:09:54.540
Pele scored eight goals.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.403
Suddenly he was famous.

00:09:58.463 --> 00:10:02.736
Thank you, Voldemort, said Pele.

00:10:02.796 --> 00:10:06.099
The World Cup Games.

00:10:06.159 --> 00:10:13.426
Pele, pele, pele, pele, called the Brazilian soccer fans.

00:10:13.486 --> 00:10:17.930
The managers of the Brazilian team listened.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:26.731
Late in 1957, The names of the new Brazilian World Cup team were on the radio.

00:10:26.791 --> 00:10:28.712
Castillo.

00:10:28.772 --> 00:10:30.454
Gilmar.

00:10:30.514 --> 00:10:32.616
Matzola.

00:10:32.676 --> 00:10:35.048
Helle.

00:10:35.108 --> 00:10:37.510
Can that be right?

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.200
Palle asked.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:41.012
They want me?

00:10:41.032 --> 00:10:45.478
He was only 17.

00:10:45.538 --> 00:10:52.104
The 1958 World Cup Games were in Sweden.

00:10:52.164 --> 00:10:55.195
Halé played very well.

00:10:55.255 --> 00:10:59.947
Brazil won their first games with no problems.

00:11:00.007 --> 00:11:04.159
Then they beat Russia to nothing.

00:11:04.219 --> 00:11:07.560
But it was a difficult game.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:11.212
Wales were a strong team too.

00:11:11.272 --> 00:11:14.243
But Halé scored a goal.

00:11:14.303 --> 00:11:17.203
And Brazil won 1-0.

00:11:17.263 --> 00:11:21.555
The game with France wasn't difficult.

00:11:21.616 --> 00:11:29.013
Brazil won 5-2, and Palais scored three goals.

00:11:29.073 --> 00:11:33.167
Now they were in the final with Sweden.

00:11:33.227 --> 00:11:39.332
Brazil didn't start well, and Sweden scored first.

00:11:39.392 --> 00:11:44.336
But then Brazil scored five goals.

00:11:44.396 --> 00:11:51.277
Two of those goals were Pellet's and Brazil won 5-2.

00:11:51.337 --> 00:11:57.629
Pellet scored six goals in his first World Cup.

00:11:57.689 --> 00:12:00.850
Brazil were the champions.

00:12:00.911 --> 00:12:05.512
Now Pellet wasn't only famous in Brazil.

00:12:05.572 --> 00:12:15.203
Pellet didn't play in the later games of the 1962 World Cup in Chile because he had an injury.

00:12:15.263 --> 00:12:22.786
He watched his team and they beat Czechoslovakia 3-1 in the final.

00:12:22.846 --> 00:12:30.672
Brazil with the champions again and Palais was very happy for the team.

00:12:30.732 --> 00:12:36.065
The 1966 World Cup was in England.

00:12:36.126 --> 00:12:40.529
Palais doesn't like remembering this championship.

00:12:40.589 --> 00:12:45.834
Usually, Brazil went to the games with 22 players.

00:12:45.894 --> 00:12:49.676
In England, they had 43.

00:12:49.736 --> 00:12:56.392
This was bad for the team because there were new players in every game.

00:12:56.452 --> 00:13:01.866
In an early game, Portugal beat them 3-1.

00:13:01.926 --> 00:13:07.478
The day after that game, Brazil went home.

00:13:07.538 --> 00:13:14.498
In 1970, the World Cup Championship was in Mexico.

00:13:14.558 --> 00:13:22.071
Pellet was only 29, but he was the old man of the Brazilian team.

00:13:22.131 --> 00:13:26.153
They beat Czechoslovakia or won.

00:13:26.213 --> 00:13:30.875
Then they played England, the World Champions.

00:13:30.935 --> 00:13:37.592
It was a very interesting game, and Brazil won 1-0.

00:13:37.652 --> 00:13:47.201
After this, they beat Romania 3-2 and Pelé scored two goals.

00:13:47.261 --> 00:13:54.244
Then they played Peru in the Jalisco Stadium and they won 4-2.

00:13:54.304 --> 00:14:00.727
Now there was only one game with Uruguay before the final.

00:14:00.787 --> 00:14:06.110
It was difficult, but Brazil won 3-1.

00:14:06.171 --> 00:14:13.483
The team went to Mexico City and waited for the final with Italy.

00:14:13.544 --> 00:14:24.729
The 1970 World Cup final started in the Aztec Stadium on the afternoon of June 21, 1970.

00:14:24.789 --> 00:14:28.881
Helle quickly scored a very good goal.

00:14:28.941 --> 00:14:35.688
There was a goal from Italy But then Brazil scored three times.

00:14:35.748 --> 00:14:39.191
They won 4-1.

00:14:39.251 --> 00:14:45.116
After the game, Helé said goodbye to World Cup soccer.

00:14:45.176 --> 00:14:47.938
People were very sorry.

00:14:47.998 --> 00:14:53.532
How many players in the world can say, I won three World Cups?

00:14:53.592 --> 00:14:54.964
They asked.

00:14:55.024 --> 00:14:57.776
There was only one answer.

00:14:57.836 --> 00:15:00.248
There was only one man.

00:15:00.308 --> 00:15:04.152
His name was Pele.

00:15:04.212 --> 00:15:07.324
A difficult girl.

00:15:07.384 --> 00:15:12.868
It was a Saturday night in 1958.

00:15:12.928 --> 00:15:19.042
Pele and Zito were in Santos again, after the World Cup.

00:15:19.102 --> 00:15:24.586
There's a girl's ball game in the stadium, Zito said.

00:15:24.647 --> 00:15:27.518
Let's go and watch.

00:15:27.578 --> 00:15:32.192
There was a young white girl at the ball game.

00:15:32.252 --> 00:15:38.016
She looked at Pele many times, and he looked at her.

00:15:38.076 --> 00:15:45.332
You're the famous Pele, and you play for Santos, she said, after the game.

00:15:45.392 --> 00:15:48.514
That's right, Pele said.

00:15:48.574 --> 00:15:51.297
Are you from the town?

00:15:51.357 --> 00:15:57.558
Yes, the girl said, but I don't like soccer.

00:15:57.618 --> 00:16:00.336
Then she walked away.

00:16:00.396 --> 00:16:02.576
Who was that?

00:16:02.637 --> 00:16:04.518
Zito asked.

00:16:04.578 --> 00:16:06.728
Palais smiled.

00:16:06.788 --> 00:16:10.580
A difficult girl, he said.

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:17.134
Palais liked the difficult girl, but he didn't know her name.

00:16:17.194 --> 00:16:20.366
He talked to her friends.

00:16:20.426 --> 00:16:24.608
Her names rosemary Colby, they said.

00:16:24.668 --> 00:16:28.238
She works in a music store.

00:16:28.298 --> 00:16:33.629
That same week Pele went to the store.

00:16:33.689 --> 00:16:36.830
Rosemary was there.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.572
They talked for some time.

00:16:39.632 --> 00:16:42.352
Then Pele asked.

00:16:42.412 --> 00:16:46.374
Can you come out with me sometimes?

00:16:46.435 --> 00:16:50.386
I'm sorry, Rosemary said.

00:16:50.446 --> 00:16:52.797
I'm only fourteen.

00:16:52.857 --> 00:16:55.709
I don't go out with boys.

00:16:55.768 --> 00:17:00.130
But come to my house one afternoon.

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:06.945
Hallé was a visitor at Rosemary's house for seven years.

00:17:07.004 --> 00:17:13.610
Then, in February 1965, they married.

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:21.337
The boy with no shoes and the difficult girl were very happy.

00:17:21.397 --> 00:17:25.166
Hallé's years with Santos.

00:17:25.226 --> 00:17:29.988
Palais played for Santos from August 1956 to October 1974.

00:17:30.008 --> 00:17:39.094
In those years, they were the number one club in Brazil and the world.

00:17:39.154 --> 00:17:47.654
They won the Brazilian Championship in 1961, 1962, 1963, 1964, and 1965.

00:17:47.674 --> 00:18:01.942
They won the South American Club Championship in 1962, 1963, and 1968.

00:18:02.002 --> 00:18:17.532
and they won the World Club Championship in the same years.

00:18:17.592 --> 00:18:25.488
Pellet and the Santos team visited many countries and played a lot of games.

00:18:25.548 --> 00:18:29.310
Sometimes this was difficult for Pellet.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:33.413
He didn't like staying in hotels all the time.

00:18:33.473 --> 00:18:37.986
He wanted to be home in Brazil with his family.

00:18:38.046 --> 00:18:46.380
Halay's final game for Santos was on October 2nd, 1974.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:49.772
The game was with Pontipreta.

00:18:49.832 --> 00:18:54.414
After a short time, Halay stopped playing.

00:18:54.474 --> 00:19:00.598
He had the ball in his hands and looked at the fans in the stadium.

00:19:00.658 --> 00:19:06.768
Thank you, he said, and he walked away from the game.

00:19:06.828 --> 00:19:09.226
We love you!"

00:19:09.286 --> 00:19:11.558
called the fans.

00:19:11.618 --> 00:19:20.564
After Santos, Pellet went to New York for a job with an American team, New York Cosmos.

00:19:20.625 --> 00:19:26.878
The job was for $4,700,000.

00:19:26.938 --> 00:19:31.572
Many people in Brazil were unhappy about this.

00:19:31.632 --> 00:19:36.316
Pellet is only going for the money, they said.

00:19:36.376 --> 00:19:38.798
but they were wrong.

00:19:38.858 --> 00:19:43.160
Pellet wanted to make soccer famous in the U.S.

00:19:43.221 --> 00:19:48.222
He did this, and his new team were very happy.

00:19:48.282 --> 00:19:53.554
Pellet stayed with New York Cosmos for three years.

00:19:53.615 --> 00:19:59.646
His final game was on October 1, 1977.

00:19:59.706 --> 00:20:03.692
It was with his old club Santos.

00:20:03.752 --> 00:20:08.878
Pele played for his new team and then for Santos.

00:20:08.938 --> 00:20:15.210
He scored a good goal and said, goodbye to soccer.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:18.511
After soccer.

00:20:18.571 --> 00:20:22.112
Pele didn't stop working.

00:20:22.172 --> 00:20:26.374
He wasn't only a good soccer player and teacher.

00:20:26.434 --> 00:20:29.364
He loved young people too.

00:20:29.424 --> 00:20:32.062
He worked for UNICEF.

00:20:32.122 --> 00:20:37.419
and talked with governments about the problems of the world's children.

00:20:37.479 --> 00:20:44.600
Then, in 1995, he started to work for the Brazilian government.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:53.262
But the world's soccer fans remember him for his two good feet and say, Thank you, Pele.

00:20:53.322 --> 00:20:56.103
Soccer champion of the world.

